They ask: “Production is broken. What do you do?”
======================================================
1. API suddenly returns 503 after deployment, but all pods appear healthy. What would you check first?
2. Database CPU reaches 100% while application CPU remains low. How would you identify the queries causing the problem?
3. HikariCP reports connection timeout, but database connections are available. What could be happening?
4. Requests are stuck for 30+ seconds with no errors in application logs. How would you find the blocked operation?
5. Kafka consumer lag keeps increasing even though consumers are running. What could be causing it?
6. Messages are processed twice after a consumer restart. How would you make processing idempotent?
7. Redis suddenly becomes unavailable. Should the application fail, bypass the cache, or use another strategy?
8. One microservice becomes slow, and soon several other services start timing out. How would you stop the cascading failure?
9. Memory usage continuously increases until the JVM crashes. What would you inspect before simply increasing heap size?
10. GC pauses suddenly increase after a new release. How would you determine whether the release caused excessive object creation?
11. Only one Kubernetes pod is slow while the others are healthy. What could cause this?
12. Load balancer returns intermittent 502 errors, but application logs show nothing unusual. Which layers would you investigate?
13. A scheduled job executes twice after scaling from one pod to five. How would you fix it?
14. Users occasionally receive stale data immediately after an update. How would you investigate database/cache consistency?
15. Database update succeeds but Kafka publishing fails. How would you guarantee the event isn’t lost?
16. Kafka publishing succeeds but the database transaction rolls back. How could consumers receive an event for data that doesn’t exist?
17. API latency increases only during peak traffic, while average CPU remains below 50%. What hidden bottlenecks would you investigate?
18. A downstream API becomes unavailable, and your retry mechanism starts generating even more traffic. How would you redesign the retry strategy?
19. After enabling parallel processing, throughput improves but the database starts failing under load. Why could this happen?
20. Everything looks healthy — CPU, memory, database and pods — but users still report random failures. How would you systematically isolate the root cause?
